// Album: Kickwerk
// Track: 05 — crankshaft
// Genre: Heavy techno / hard kick studies
// Tempo / CPM: 157 BPM (setcpm 39.25)
// Bass concept: A1 sub still locked to the kick's *4 pulse — the straight motion the crank converts.
// Kick character: hard shape, mid lpf — the constant the rest of the machine has to translate.
// Musical idea: A crankshaft turns one straight motion into rotation — the kick stays a plain four-on-
//   the-floor "piston," while a metal hit rides a euclidean 3-against-4 on top of it, always landing
//   somewhere different relative to the kick. Two mechanisms, two time signatures, one engine.
// Strudel focus: s("metal").euclid(3,4) layered against a static kick pulse — the polyrhythm is the point.
// Visualisation: ._punchcard({ cycles: 4, vertical: true }) — vertical reads the two grids crossing.

setcpm(39.25)

stack(

  // ── KICK — the straight stroke ───────────────────────────────────
  s("bd*4")
    .shape(0.5).distort(1.1).lpf(195)
    .gain(0.9)
    .color("red")
    ._punchcard({ cycles: 4, vertical: true }),

  // ── SUB — locked body ─────────────────────────────────────────────
  note("a1*4")
    .sound("sine").attack(0.001).release(0.14).shape(0.1)
    .gain(0.56)
    .color("navy"),

  // ── CRANK — metal hit in 3-against-4 ──────────────────────────────
  s("metal").euclid(3, 4)
    .gain(0.3).hpf(1200).room(0.22)
    .color("silver"),

  // ── HATS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  s("~ hh ~ hh").gain(0.24).hpf(7000)
    .color("yellow")
)
